{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Registration.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Registration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender add on registration blender add on registration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Registration.md","fileName":"Blender Add-On Registration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Add-On Registration","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Add-On Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Architecture","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Registration.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Registration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender add on registration blender add on registration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Registration.md","fileName":"Blender Add-On Registration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Add-On Registration","heading":"Blender Add-On Registration","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Registration makes an add-on's classes and properties available to Blender; unregistration removes them when the add-on is disabled or reloaded. Dependent classes should be registered in a logical order and unregistered in reverse order so that no component is removed while another still relies on it.\n\nThe source describes both explicit per-class calls and module-wide helpers available in Blender 2.78c. Its development template favors a clean slate before registering newly evaluated classes. Regardless of version-specific functions, reliable add-ons make activation repeatable, cleanup complete, and accidental duplicate registration visible.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Architecture","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"propertie